Z||000007||onfire||06-21-2001||03:13 AM||||Taken straight from Archie's site<P>"Pricing<P>For the complete conversion (Steps #1, #2 & #3) Introductory Price $ 3195.00*<BR>For conversion without paint (Steps #1 & #2) Introductory Price $ 2795.00<BR>For the conversion to the top only (Step #1 you do the interior & paint at your leisure) Introductory Price $ 2395.00<P>* This price can vary depending on your paint choices.<P>The complete process takes 3 to 4 weeks to complete and is by appointment only.<P>You are urged to make your appointment early."||||reg||1
Z||000008||fyerstarter||06-21-2001||03:39 AM||||Ever since I saw your car for sale on Archies site about a year ago I have been in love with it. The only two things I would changed about it would be get rid of the side trim, it would look bad-ass shaved.. or if nothing else painted to match. Black side molding is just not befitting of such and exotic looking machine. And personally I would like to see the ass end lowered. I don't know if the jacked up hotrod look is what your goin for but it's a bit too stinkbug for my tastes. Still by far the nicest Fiero I have ever seen. Your a lucky man.||||reg||1
